WEBVTT

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.230
So good!

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.200
Hey, you've been drinking too much, you know.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.190
You have some too, Elch!

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.950
Th-Thank you, Emerada.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.740
Hey, miss?

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.350
What is it, Melinda?

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.930
Have some of this, too!

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:29.080
Oh! Looks tasty!

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.330
You're putting me in a great mood!

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.470
There's clean streets, delicious food,

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:41.220
and kind villagers here, too.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:43.850
We're happy to hear that.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.600
Those of us here in Coconono Village

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.800
are able to live in comfort 
thanks to our lord,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:55.910
Oslo El Gustave, 
and Emperor Lindworm Von Freyjagard.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:00.940
We're always talking to each other
about how we'd like to share

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.400
this happiness with as many people as possible.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:09.370
Mama always goes to extra lengths when 
we get travelers and makes too much food!

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:12.200
Melinda, you don't need to tell them that.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.360
Oh, sorry!

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:21.640
I never thought the world could be a whole
different place in the very next region.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.980
You can say that again!

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:26.520
Don't be shy. We still have plenty more!

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.230
Then maybe I will have a refill!

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:32.670
Sure!

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.490
Yay!

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.390
<b>High School Prodigies Have It Easy
Even In Another World!</b>

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.840
<b>It Seems Shinobu Has
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\ha Shinobi's Intuition!</b>

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:18.600
I drank, I ate, and now I...

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.590
take a nap!

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.720
Are you okay?

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.970
I'm sorry about this.
 The villagers got too excited.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:32.670
Don't be. She'll be absolutely, perfectly fine!

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:33.990
I see.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:39.560
We don't have any other guests today, 
so we hope you have a great stay.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:44.570
H-Hey.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:45.740
Hm?

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.580
Y-You two should, um...

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.210
hurry up and leave the village.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.720
Melinda!

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.660
Let's get going!

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.340
C-Coming.

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:04.300
What was that?

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:12.180
Man, I still can't believe there's a village
this well-off within the empire.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.680
If they're comfortable as is,

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:19.640
then they might not agree with
the teachings of the Seven-Light Faith.

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:22.400
What should we do then, Shinobu?

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.660
Well, in that case...

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:36.410
Well, how do you feel?

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:37.790
Sobered up now?

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.500
Wh-Wh-What the hell are you doing?!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:42.960
Huh?

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.380
You're already sober?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.820
Of course I am.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:48.780
There's no way a shinobi
would get drunk off so little.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.390
Th-Then why were you putting on that act?

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:54.470
Because something wasn't right.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.640
Huh?

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.030
Didn't you notice?

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:02.570
The people in this village kept 
encouraging us to eat and drink,

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:06.060
but they barely even touched 
the food themselves,

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:09.240
even though they were all starving.

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.790
Starving?

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.790
Yes, starving.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.290
They hid it with makeup and such,

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.670
but their skin was rough and dried out,

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:23.100
and their eyes were so jaundiced 
even an amateur could spot it.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.930
Those are classic symptoms of malnutrition.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.970
What do you mean?

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.750
When we first entered this village,

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:34.250
I only had a vague sense that 
something was wrong, but now I know.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:37.880
Follow me.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.930
Listen, El.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:54.950
This is the truth behind this village.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.170
What is this...

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.590
They lure travelers into their inn,

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:03.040
fill them up on food and 
drink until they can't move,

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.670
and do this.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:08.020
They're killing them and 
stealing all of their money?

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:12.720
Looks like that's not all.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:16.750
This village feels more like 
a den of thieves

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:19.780
that's literally sucking their victims dry.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.730
Wait, did we just eat...

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.920
You don't have to worry about that.

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:29.900
What we ate was regular animal meat.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:35.330
All villagers, out of your homes!

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:40.330
The Silver Knight, Jeanne Do Leblanc, 
is here for the inspection!

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:44.440
All right, everyone's here.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:45.630
Now, then...

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:48.380
The greeting!

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:52.060
Thank you very much for your good work today.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:57.640
We commoners were able to 
enjoy another happy day today.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:02.150
All of which is thanks 
to His Imperial Majesty!

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:03.420
What?

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:07.150
Everyone, correct your posture!

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:21.120
All good! You may go home!

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.630
Wait! You there, parent and child!

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:28.710
Yes, what is it?

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:31.470
There is dirt on your daughter's right sleeve!

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:33.840
Huh?!

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:41.280
Your attire must always be free of
dirt and fraying, clean and beautiful.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:44.480
Anyone who lives in His Imperial Majesty's lands

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.940
must strive to maintain 
those minimum standards.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:49.530
Bring her here!

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.650
We shall dole out the punishment!

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:55.470
What is this? 
What's the point of all this?

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:56.670
Who knows?

00:07:56.670 --> 00:08:00.910
But, sometimes, those who hold 
absolute authority over people

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:05.690
will do things that no normal 
person could ever understand.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.840
Mama! Mama!

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.130
P-Please wait!

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:12.340
A child's mistake is the parent's mistake!

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:14.830
If you must punish anyone, please punish me!

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:16.600
You stopped smiling.

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:20.720
As the people protected by 
His Imperial Majesty himself,

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:23.720
you must show your gratitude to him

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:26.060
by maintaining a smile at all times.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.580
These are the laws of Duke Gustave.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.480
Smile! Can you not smile?!

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.630
This is awful!

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:48.600
All this over a little stain on her clothes?!

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:49.920
What are you planning to do?

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.380
Save them!

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:55.880
Those people tried to deceive 
and murder us, you know.

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:59.140
But that girl...

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:01.860
She was trying to warn us.

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:03.890
She told us to run.

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.030
So...

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:10.270
I understand how you feel, El.

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:14.390
But if that's how it's gonna be,
then I have a plan.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.460
Hello, hello!

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.880
Who are you?

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.960
If you keep going, she really will die.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.880
So could you knock it off?

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:40.980
That uniquely shaped weapon is a shuriken...

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:45.480
Are you a ninja from Yamato Empire?

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:51.610
So you've come out to rescue 
that young girl, have you?

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:52.820
A real daredevil.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.320
Hey, care to make a deal with me?

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:57.220
A deal?

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:02.200
Surrounded by all those men of yours,
even I'm not likely to win.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:07.790
But I will be able to take over 
half of them down with me.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:10.540
That includes you, by the way.

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:16.420
However, if you'll promise to stop 
your cruelty toward that child,

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:19.050
then I'll let you capture me
without a fight.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:24.040
Very well.

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:26.060
Release the girl!

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.030
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.940
Melinda!

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:31.370
Thanks.

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.190
Seize her!

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:37.000
Take that woman with us!

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:42.530
You're going to go rescue them?!

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:43.550
That's right.

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:48.410
Those guys might even take me straight 
to the heart of our enemy here, too.

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:53.790
Just make sure you tell Micchan that 
I let myself be captured, okay?

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.110
<i>Shinobu...</i>

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:09.020
<i>Well, what to do next...</i>

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:11.800
<i>They didn't take me all the way
to the lord's castle,</i>

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:14.970
<i>but I should be able to gather 
some information in this one, too.</i>

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:20.990
<i>I could break out of these easily,</i>

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:23.120
<i>kidnap the owner of this castle,</i>

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.620
<i>and have them tell me
everything they know about Gustave.</i>

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:29.670
<i>That would be the most 
efficient thing to do...</i>

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:31.500
Open it.

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:45.800
Torturing her already?

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:47.560
You go stand outside.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:48.310
Huh?!

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:53.100
B-But isn't it too dangerous to leave 
you alone with her, Captain Jeanne?

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:54.960
I'm a woman, too.

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:59.190
I don't want to let a man watch 
a woman being brutally tormented.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.570
You don't need to show an 
enemy that kind of mercy.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:07.830
Are you suggesting you'd rather 
I beat you out of here by force?

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.360
P-Pardon me!

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:12.060
Um...

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:17.250
It might not be my place to say this,

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:21.970
but aren't you taking a shinobi too lightly?

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:43.040
Thank you so much!

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:44.700
For saving my daughter!

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:48.910
I saw the basement of this inn.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:53.160
You all were planning on 
murdering us, weren't you?

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.270
And not just murder us...

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:00.550
Please forgive us.

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:03.880
In your dreams! Why are you doing that?!

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:08.010
Because we have no choice...

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:15.050
If we don't do it, we can't survive...

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:23.920
Coconono Village was originally 
a small farming village {}

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:25.770
that made its livelihood growing wheat.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:30.030
However, the moment Gustave became our lord,

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:32.340
he issued the beautification decree.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:39.620
It meant that we had to ensure that both
we and our streets were beautiful.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:44.220
Of course, all the expenses for that 
had to come out of our own pockets...

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:49.210
That left our village completely penniless...

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:53.630
We couldn't get muddy, so we could
no longer work the fields properly.

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:56.360
We spent every day fighting 
against starvation,

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:58.870
eating everything we could possibly eat...

00:13:59.430 --> 00:14:02.540
When there was finally 
nothing else left, we...

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.050
Even though we were poor,

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:12.980
as long as we had our beloved families
and a little bit of food on the table,

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:15.180
we could share real happiness...

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:19.710
But now it's all come to this...

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:21.680
I can't smile anymore.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:25.210
There's no happiness left!

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:29.970
What you've done can never be forgiven.

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:31.300
However...

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:39.650
Thank you for saving that young girl earlier.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:43.480
Uh, what exactly is going on here?

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:46.740
My name is Jeanne Do Leblanc.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:51.990
I'm an Imperial Silver Knight 
in service to Count Blumhardt,

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:57.430
and a member of the Azure Brigade that worries
for the future of the Gustave region.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:02.960
If you have come from the Yamato Empire 
to infiltrate this region of Gustave,

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:06.280
then you and the Azure Brigade share 
a common enemy in Duke Fastidious,

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:08.630
Oslo El Gustave.

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:11.760
They say the enemy of my enemy is my friend.

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:17.770
Would you be willing to lend us your aid
and help the people suffering here?

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:24.120
Oh, what a beautiful and gallant form!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.890
This golden statue

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:30.810
will surely display His Majesty's 
glory to the people.

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:33.050
The statue will be placed at the center of

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:36.280
the grand fountain in the 
central plaza of the imperial capital.

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:38.320
Wonderful.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:41.390
Now, let us make four more of these

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:45.020
and place one in each of the lands
in the cardinal directions.

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:48.300
Start procuring the gold at once.

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:53.240
I-If I may offer my humble opinion,

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:56.040
making just one of these golden statues

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:59.070
has placed a heavy burden upon 
the people within your domain...

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:02.940
I have heard that it's not 
uncommon for your people

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:06.400
to eat the flesh of travelers or 
relatives to stave off starvation...

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:10.640
If we were to try and create four more 
statues while they're in that state, then...

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:12.920
My people will perish?

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:15.530
Y-Yes, sir.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.230
That is fine.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:22.710
Knights prove their loyalty to 
His Majesty through deeds of arms.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:26.800
Nobles prove their loyalty to 
His Majesty through proper governance

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.210
of the lands they're entrusted with.

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:34.860
So how then, do lowborn 
peasants prove their loyalty?

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.470
There is but one answer:

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:40.220
through dying for His Majesty.

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:43.730
Do you understand, Oscar?

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:49.080
By the way, have we managed to suppress 
the rebellion that occurred in Findolf?

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:50.110
Sir!

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:53.100
Once winter is over and
the path for our army clears,

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:57.570
100,000 troops are ready 
to descend upon Findolf.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.700
When winter is over?

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:04.960
Buchwald and Arclide haven't marched yet?

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.960
Huh? No, sir...

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:12.460
So you're telling me we have 
allowed those pests to

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:19.560
trample over His Imperial Majesty's 
sacred land for over a month?!

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.600
What a disgrace!

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.760
What ineptitude!

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:28.840
My deep apologies, Your Imperial Majesty!

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.570
Now I am angry.

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:42.020
It is time to use L'age Soleil!

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:05.880
Hup...

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:07.530
<i>Danger...</i>

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:14.580
<i>Danger is approaching the seven heroes.</i>

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:19.380
<i>I need your help.</i>

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:25.510
<i>Please, you must guide them.</i>

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:27.700
What was that voice?

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.420
The seven heroes?

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:40.180
Those pests devouring 
the lands of Freyjagard!

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:45.620
They shall know the heat of 
the rage burning within me!

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:55.360
<i>Help us...</i>

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.070
<i>Help us!</i>

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:00.700
<i>Please... help us!</i>

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.080
<i>Emergency!</i>

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:04.240
<i>Emergency!</i>

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.260
<i>Sending an emergency broadcast 
to all communication terminals!</i>

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:09.460
<i>We have an emergency, bear!</i>

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:11.460
<i>Altitude, 6,000 meters!</i>

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.860
<i>Distance, 200 kilometers!</i>

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:18.460
<i>A flying object is rapidly approaching 
Dormundt from the south-southeast, bear!</i>

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:23.400
<i>Ringo, I understand what's going 
on from the emergency broadcast.</i>

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:24.470
<i>What's this flying object?</i>

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:28.830
I don't have any exact details on it, but...

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:33.210
<i>From its angle and trajectory, we have a 
rough idea of its point of origin, bear!</i>

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:35.320
<i>It came from the Gustave region!</i>

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:37.820
A-At this rate,

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:41.950
<i>it will land right in the middle of Dormundt!</i>

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:48.200
Then this is probably
Oslo El Gustave's Heaven's Flames.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.160
Wha?!

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:50.670
Ringo.

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:51.920
<i>Leave it to me!</i>

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.920
Bearabbit, fire the anti-air missiles!

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:55.920
<i>Roger that, bear!</i>

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:20.890
<i>It's no use, bear!</i>

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:22.750
<i>It didn't work at all, bear!</i>

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.260
Why not?!

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:28.280
<i>I imagine some kind of 
magic acted to protect it.</i>

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:32.810
<i>If it's unharmed after that, then it's going 
to be beary difficult to shoot it down!</i>

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:36.700
<i>Ringo, were there any changes 
to the spear's trajectory</i>

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:39.150
<i>and predicted landing point 
after we intercepted it?</i>

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:40.630
H-Hold on.

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:43.130
I'm calculating now.

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:47.640
It's been diverted to the noble residences
on the southeastern block.

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:54.390
Mikogami Tsukasa

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:52.480
<i>Attack it with missiles to
further divert it outside the city.</i>

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:54.390
<i>The farther away, the better.</i>

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:57.020
S-Sure, but...

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.070
W-Will we be okay?

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:06.570
I've spent this last month researching 
Gustave's Heaven's Flames.

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:09.980
From that, I suspect these Heaven's Flames

00:21:09.980 --> 00:21:12.810
are closer to an incendiary 
bomb than an explosive.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:16.730
So long as as we avoid a direct hit,
it's not that big a threat.

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:17.710
Please do it.

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:19.510
All right!

00:21:20.070 --> 00:21:23.640
Bearabbit, let's use our missiles
to redirect that spear

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:25.610
into the ocean outside the city!

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.090
<i>Bear!</i>

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:46.780
<i>It's going well, bear!</i>

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.120
<i>Last one!</i>

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:50.540
<i>Let's finish it with the fourth round, bear!</i>

00:21:57.450 --> 00:21:58.330
No way!

00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:00.590
<i>It evaded it, bear!</i>

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:01.980
<i>Oh, no, bear!</i>

00:22:01.980 --> 00:22:04.460
<i>It's going to impact, bear!</i>
